---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import portraitImage from '../assets/images/profile-1.png';
---

<Layout
	title="About Andrew Smith | UX Design Leader & Senior Product Designer"
	description="Andrew Smith, twenty years across product design, front-end development, and UX leadership. Based in Adelaide, South Australia. Available for senior UX and design leadership roles."
>
	<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>

	<div class="page">
		<SiteHeader />

		<main id="main-content">
			<section class="hero">
				<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
				<div class="hero-layout">
					<div class="hero-copy">
						<h1 class="display-title">Senior UX designer and team manager based in Adelaide.</h1>
						<p class="hero-text">
							Twenty years across product design, front-end development, and UX team management.
							Interested in how teams make design decisions and how to build the practice around them.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="hero-portrait-wrap">
						<Image
							class="hero-portrait"
							src={portraitImage}
							alt="Portrait of Andrew Smith"
							loading="eager"
							decoding="async"
							widths={[320, 480, 640]}
							sizes="(max-width: 980px) 100vw, 32vw"
						/>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="editorial-section">
				<div class="section-rail">
					<p class="section-kicker">Background</p>
				</div>
				<div class="story-block">
					<p>
						Started as a self-taught web designer and front-end developer, building websites for clients across agency, media, and corporate environments. Moved into UX at the University of Adelaide, where I led UX practice and introduced a design system approach across the university's digital products.
					</p>
					<p>
						Seven years at RAA after that, first as the senior designer across travel, insurance, member portal, payments, and renewals, then as UX Manager responsible for the team, the practice, and delivery quality. Two decades of real products, real users, and real engineering constraints.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="editorial-section">
				<div class="section-rail">
					<p class="section-kicker">How I Work</p>
				</div>
				<div class="story-block">
					<p>
						Research before design. I work within Agile product squads alongside product managers, engineers, analytics teams, and business stakeholders — reviewing what the data is showing, attending roadmap and vision discussions, facilitating discovery workshops, and bringing customer and usability evidence into the decisions the team is making. The design work is grounded in that context, not separate from it.
					</p>
					<p>
						Design system thinking from the start. Consistency comes from captured decisions, documented components, and governance that maintains them. When the system is working, product and engineering teams can move faster and the design team spends more time on the problems that actually need solving.
					</p>
					<p>
						Close to delivery and to product. I write clear specs, work alongside engineers as a peer — starting in code means feasibility conversations are grounded in shared understanding — and stay involved through build, QA, and the measurement that follows.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="editorial-section">
				<div class="section-rail">
					<p class="section-kicker">Available</p>
				</div>
				<div class="story-block">
					<p>
						Open to senior product designer, UX lead, design management, and product owner roles in Adelaide and remotely. <a href="mailto:asmithdigital@gmail.com">asmithdigital@gmail.com</a> or 0400 895 354.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="pm-card-section">
				<div class="pm-card">
					<div class="pm-card-header">
						<svg class="pm-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
						<p class="pm-card-title">Currently studying product management</p>
					</div>
					<p class="pm-card-body">Product management is the discipline responsible for deciding what gets built, for whom, and why — balancing customer needs, business viability, and technical feasibility. A product manager works as part of a trio with design and engineering, owning the problem space so the team can focus on solving the right thing rather than building the wrong thing well.</p>
					<p class="pm-card-body">I am studying it because I have been working inside that trio for over a decade — contributing the design and customer insight seat alongside product managers and engineers. Understanding the formal discipline more deeply makes that partnership more effective and opens the path to taking on product responsibilities directly.</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page {
		position: relative;
		width: min(calc(100% - 3rem), 78rem);
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 1.25rem 0 5rem;
	}

	.eyebrow,
	.section-kicker {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		line-height: 1.4;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.hero {
		padding: 6rem 0 4rem;
	}

	.hero-layout {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(15rem, 20rem);
		gap: 2.5rem;
		align-items: start;
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}

	.hero-copy {
		max-width: 52rem;
	}

	.eyebrow,
	.section-kicker {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--muted-foreground);
		font-style: normal;
	}

	.hero-text,
	.story-block p {
		font-size: 1.08rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.hero-text {
		max-width: 44rem;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	.hero-portrait-wrap {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: flex-end;
		align-self: start;
		padding-top: 0.35rem;
	}

	.hero-portrait {
		width: min(100%, 20rem);
		height: auto;
		display: block;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		box-shadow: 0 18px 40px rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.08);
	}

	.editorial-section {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 16rem minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 2rem;
		padding: 2.5rem 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.section-rail {
		align-self: start;
	}

	.story-block {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		max-width: 52rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 1100px) {
		.hero-layout {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 1.75rem;
			align-items: start;
		}

		.hero-copy {
			max-width: 100%;
		}

		.hero-text {
			max-width: 42rem;
		}

		.hero-portrait-wrap {
			justify-content: flex-start;
			padding-top: 0;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.page {
			width: min(calc(100% - 1.5rem), 78rem);
			padding-top: 1rem;
		}

		.hero {
			padding: 4rem 0 3rem;
		}

		.editorial-section {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.hero-text,
		.story-block p {
			font-size: 1.05rem;
		}

		.hero-portrait {
			width: min(100%, 16rem);
		}
	}
	.pm-card-section { margin-top: 2rem; padding-bottom: 3rem; }
	.pm-card { background: #eef4ff; border: 1.5px solid #93b8f5; border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem; }
	.pm-card-header { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
	.pm-icon { width: 1.25rem; height: 1.25rem; color: #1a4a8a; flex-shrink: 0; }
	.pm-card-title { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 800; color: #1a4a8a; margin: 0; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
	.pm-card-body { font-size: 0.96rem; line-height: 1.65; color: #2a3a5a; margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
	.pm-card-body:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
</style>
